SECTION A — OVERCLAIM REGISTER
Severity: P0 = blocks publication; P1 = must fix before submission;
P2 = cosmetic (sampled, not exhaustive).

----------------------------- P0 FINDINGS --------------------------------------

P0-1  RESULTS.md L88–L99 — the main curve theorem is FALSE as stated for
      N ≡ 1,2,3 (mod 4), N ≥ 5.
      Quote L92: "S_max(N, F) = 2 + 2 · min(N, 4) · F, for 0 ≤ F ≤
      (S_cap − 2)/(2·min(N,4))" and L99: "N ≥ 4: S_max = 2 + 8F (cap S = 4 at
      F = 1/4)".
      Why false: PROOFS.md §6–§8 (Theorems 2–3) prove the curve bends at
      F = 1/N, not 1/4, for N = 5,6,7: S_max(5,F) = 16/5 + 2F on [1/5, 2/5]
      so S_max(5, 1/4) = 3.7 < 4; S_max(6,F) = 8/3 + 4F on [1/6, 1/3];
      S_max(7,F) = 16/7 + 6F on [1/7, 2/7]. The exact cap is F(S=4;N) =
      ⌈N/4⌉/N = 2/5, 1/3, 2/7 for N = 5,6,7 — not 1/4. Evidence: audit1.out
      Part A (Fraction certificate over all multisets) and capregion.out
      (independent LP cross-check: S_max(5,0.25) = 3.7 to 1.8e-15).
      Note: the headline F* = (√2−1)/min(N,4) is UNAFFECTED (it only uses the
      curve on [0, F*] ⊂ [0, 1/N]); this finding is about the stated curve and
      cap, not the headline.
      Fix: replace L88–L99 with Theorem 3's exact curves (N = 2..8) plus the
      general statements "S_max(N,F) = 2+8F on [0,1/N] for all N ≥ 4" and
      "cap F(S=4;N) = ⌈N/4⌉/N (Theorem 2), with the full piecewise-linear
      curves for N = 5,6,7 in the supplement". This is PROOFS §11 item 1 —
      not yet applied to RESULTS.md.

----------------------------- P1 FINDINGS --------------------------------------

P1-1  RESULTS.md L116–L118, L146, L161–L164 — the "infinite / all-N class"
      claim is asserted but not proved as written, and "uniform source, finite
      or not" is ill-defined.
      Quote L116–118: "any local deterministic CHSH model (with a uniform
      source, finite or not) that reaches the maximal quantum violation must
      fine-tune at least one of its conditional source distributions by ≥
      ~10.4% in TV"; L161–164: "This 2 + 8F is a genuine theorem about the
      whole (infinite, all-N) class, not just the finite samples: it is a
      TV/Lipschitz argument that does not use finiteness of N."
      Problem: PROOFS.md §5 proves S ≤ 2+8F for FINITE N only (via Theorem 1).
      The measure-theoretic extension is true but written nowhere. Also a
      uniform distribution exists only on finite sets; the phrase "uniform
      source, finite or not" has no meaning for general λ-spaces. Key fact the
      fix should state: the bound does NOT use uniformity at all — it holds for
      ANY source ρ with F = max_ab TV(p(·|ab)‖ρ).
      Fix (one line, add as a proposition to PROOFS.md): for any local
      deterministic model on an arbitrary probability space (Λ,ρ), S ≤ 2+8F.
      Proof: pointwise C(q_λ) ∈ {−2,+2} ⇒ S0 = ∫C dρ ≤ 2; and by TV duality,
      |E[ab] − μ_ab| = |∫ σq (dp_ab − dρ)| ≤ 2·TV(p_ab‖ρ) ≤ 2F for f with
      range [−1,1]. Then reword RESULTS: "any local deterministic CHSH model,
      on any hidden-variable space and with any source distribution ρ — the
      bound does not use uniformity — …". Until written, restrict the claim to
      finite N. (This is the single true assertion/proof mismatch in the
      package; see B.6.)

