P2-6  PROOFS.md §9.5 L314 "patterns {M_A, M_C, M_D}" — typo. The gauge of
      ns_solN3_{u,v}.npy gives per-state product patterns {M_A, M_B, M_D}
      (verified by hand: (−,+,+,−), (+,−,+,−), (+,+,+,+); no CHSH symmetry maps
      one set to the other). The N=3 table itself is correct (referee re-
      derived S = 2√2 and all four NS residuals = 0 by hand; see B.8).
P2-7  PROOFS.md §2 (L63–66) Lemma 1 achievability wording: "move mass δ … if
      F ≥ m/N take p = point mass on a single +1 entry". Two gaps: (a) for δ ∈
      (1/N, m/N] the moved mass must be spread over ⌈δN⌉ source states (one
      state can supply at most 1/N); (b) a point mass has TV = (N−1)/N, which
      exceeds F when m/N ≤ F < (N−1)/N; the correct saturating p is any
      distribution supported on the +1 set with total moved mass exactly m/N
      (TV = m/N). The lemma STATEMENT is correct (referee re-derived it); fix
      the paragraph.
P2-8  PROOFS.md §12 L398 lists "Step 3: literature sweep" as remaining, but
      literature_check.out is complete (dated 2026-08-23) — stale; mark done.
P2-9  RESULTS.md L31–32 "a precise, falsifiable interpretation of 'how
      conspiratorial'" — rhetorical overreach; a mathematical minimum is not
      itself a falsifiable prediction. Optional softening to "a quantitative
      benchmark".
P2-10 RESULTS.md L139–142 "This directly addresses a claim in BHL … that some
      measurement-independence violations are 'signalling in principle.'" —
      positioning risk: BHL's notion is causal-structure-based (their §7:
      "Charlie has in principle the ability to prepare the required non-
      quantum distributions"), while our result concerns OBSERVABLE marginals
