================================================================================
SECTION B — PROOF-GAP AUDIT (independent re-derivation)
Method: each step of PROOFS.md re-derived by hand; witness tables recomputed
with independent plain arithmetic (python one-liners on the stated constants,
not the project scripts); audit1.py's certificate logic inspected line by
line; every .out artifact cross-referenced. No heavy computation re-run.

B.1  Lemma 1 (exact per-row TV optimum) — CORRECT.
     Upper bounds: with d = p − ρ, Σd = 0: (TV bound) |d·f| ≤ Σ|d_λ| =
     2·TV(p‖ρ) ≤ 2F; (mass bound) M⁻ := Σ_{f=−1} d_λ ≥ −m/N since each term
     ≥ −1/N, and d·f = M⁺ − M⁻ = −2M⁻ ⇒ d·f ≤ 2m/N; symmetrically d·f ≥
     −2k/N. Hence max p·f ≤ μ + 2·min(F, m/N), min by symmetry. Edge cases
     k=0 or m=0: f constant, p·f ≡ ±1 = μ. All verified.
     Achievability: correct as a claim; the proof paragraph has the two
     wording gaps of P2-7 (spreading over ⌈δN⌉ states for δ ∈ (1/N, m/N];
     point mass has TV (N−1)/N, not m/N). With the corrected construction,
     d·f = 2δ and TV(p‖ρ) = δ hold exactly. No downstream effect.

B.2  Theorem 1 (exact finite-maximum formula) — ALL FOUR STEPS VERIFIED.
     (i) Multi-affine ⇒ vertex maximum: standard coordinate-wise linearity;
         correct. "Swapping the maxima" is a plain max over a product space
         (no minimax theorem needed); correct.
     (ii) Gauge reduction: S depends on (u,v) only through q_ab(λ) =
         u[a,λ]v[b,λ]; per-state simultaneous sign flip fixes all q's; two
         vertices with the same pattern assignment give identical LP values.
         Correct.
     (iii) Realizability: referee verified the construction — set u[0]=+1,
         v[0]=q00, v[1]=q01, u[1]=q00·q10; then u[1]v[0] = q10 ✓ and
         u[1]v[1] = q00·q01·q10 = q11 (using even parity) ✓. All 8 even-
         parity patterns realizable. The "no degeneracy" relabeling-invariance
         argument is correct (uniform ρ + symmetric TV constraint).
     (iv) Row separability: the LP decomposes into 4 independent per-row TV-
         ball LPs; Lemma 1 with f_λ = σ_ab·q_ab(λ) gives exactly g_ab(F) =
         2·min(F, n_ab/N) for 0 < n_ab < N and 0 otherwise. The "no σ sign"
         claim is CORRECT: each row is optimized in its own σ_ab-direction, so
         every contribution to S is non-negative.
     Multiset counts C(8+N−1,N) = 36/120/330/792/1716/3432/6435 for N=2..8
     verified by hand; N=9: 11440 ✓ (PROOFS §8).
     Certificate logic (audit1.py): per-cell affine lines + upper hull via
     monotone chain — inspected; standard and correct. One dependency to note:
     the certificate ASSUMES Lemma 1's formula (it does not re-prove it); since
     the referee has now hand-verified Lemma 1, the chain is sound. The LP
     pipeline (phase1/2/3.py, verify.py) provides an independent float
     cross-check of the same formula.

B.3  Theorem 2 (cap F(S=4;N) = ⌈N/4⌉/N) — VERIFIED.
     Necessity: S=4 ⇔ E[ab] = σ_ab ∀ab (|E[ab]| ≤ 1, equality case of
     S = Σ σ_ab E[ab] ≤ 4); by Lemma 1 row ab reaches σ_ab iff F ≥ n_ab/N
     (0 < n_ab < N) or n_ab = 0; hence F(S=4;N) = min_Q max_ab n_ab/N ✓.
     Parity lemma: prod(σ) = −1 vs prod(q) = +1 ⇒ each λ misses at least one
     class (an odd number ≥ 1) ⇒ Σ_ab n_ab ≥ N ⇒ max_ab n_ab ≥ ⌈N/4⌉ ✓.
     Sufficiency: round-robin Q_N has n-entries in {⌊N/4⌋, ⌈N/4⌉}; at F =
     ⌈N/4⌉/N every row can be supported on its correct class (TV = n_ab/N ≤
     F) ⇒ S = 4 ✓.
     Values N=2..8: 1/2, 1/3, 1/4, 2/5, 1/3, 2/7, 1/4 — recomputed by hand;
     all match audit1.out Part A (which asserts equality with the exhaustive
     min over multisets).

B.4  Corollary 2 (headline F* = (√2−1)/min(N,4)) — VERIFIED.
     Lower bound: S ≤ 2+8F and 2 + 8·(√2−1)/4 = 2√2 exactly ✓.
     Achievability case check N = 4k+r: referee recomputed the thresholds
     k ≥ (√2−1)/(4(2−√2)) = 0.17678 (r=1), (√2−1)/(2(2−√2)) = 0.35355 (r=2),
     3(√2−1)/(4(2−√2)) = 0.53033 (r=3); PROOFS's "0.18 / 0.35 / 0.53" are
     correct roundings and k ≥ 1 in each case (r=0 trivial; the r-cases with
     k=0 give N=1,2,3 which are handled separately). Hence min(F*, n_ab/N) =
     F* on all four rows of Q_N and S_max(N,F*) ≥ 2 + 8F* = 2√2 ✓. The
     feasibility inequality ⌊N/4⌋ ≥ (√2−1)N/4 is machine-verified for N=4..999
     (ns_general.out Part A). Float cross-check: audit1.out Part B, S_max(N,
     F*) = 2.828427124746 for N=2..6; margin note (0 for N=2,3,5,6 — multiple
     optimal Q's; 0.207 for N=4) consistent with the certificate.

B.5  Theorem 3 (exact curves N=2..8) — VERIFIED WHERE CHEAP.
     All breakpoint values checked by hand: N=5: S(1/5) = 18/5 ✓, segment
     16/5+2F continuous at 1/5 (16/5+2/5 = 18/5 ✓) and hits 4 at F=2/5
     (16/5+4/5 = 4 ✓); N=6: S(1/6) = 10/3 ✓, 8/3+4F continuous (8/3+2/3 =
     10/3 ✓), 4 at F=1/3 ✓; N=7: S(1/7) = 22/7 ✓, 16/7+6F continuous (16/7+
     6/7 = 22/7 ✓), 4 at F=2/7 ✓; N=8: two cells both on 2+8F (n=(2,2,2,2)
     stays active through k=1) ✓. All match audit1.out Part A exactly.
     Independent LP cross-checks exist: capregion.out (N=5 F=0.2/0.25/0.3 →
     3.6/3.7/3.8, |diff| ≤ 1.8e-15; N=6 F=0.2 → 8/3+4·0.2 to 0.0). The §6
     statement "S_max(5,¼) = 16/5 + ¼ = 3.7 < 4" is thus confirmed both ways.

B.6  Corollary (global bound S ≤ 2+8F) — VERIFIED FOR FINITE N; EXTENSION
     MISSING (see A/P1-1).
     Referee enumerated all 8 even-parity patterns by hand: C(q) ∈ {+2,+2,
     +2,+2,−2,−2,−2,−2} (the four +2's are exactly the miss-types M_A..M_D)
     ⇒ S0 = (1/N)Σ C(q_λ) ≤ 2 ✓. Per-row |E[ab] − μ_ab| ≤ 2·min(F, n_ab/N) ≤
     2F by Lemma 1 (both max and min deviations) ✓. Tightness on [0, 1/N] for
     every N ≥ 4 via Q_N (all four rows active there) ✓. The measure-
     theoretic extension to arbitrary λ-spaces is one line — pointwise C(q_λ)
     ∈ {±2} ⇒ ∫C dρ ≤ 2, and TV duality |∫f dp − ∫f dρ| ≤ 2·TV(p‖ρ) for f
     with range [−1,1] — but it is NOT written anywhere in PROOFS.md. This is
     the only true assertion/proof mismatch in the package (RESULTS L161–164
     asserts the infinite-class form).

B.7  Theorem 4 (NS, N=2: S_NS(2,F) = 2 for ALL F ∈ [0,½]) — CERTIFICATE
     LOGIC VERIFIED.
     For each of the 256 vertices: the four NS equations force t-equalities
     exactly when the corresponding response is nonconstant in that setting
     (referee checked the derivation, e.g. A-side a=0 with u[0,·] nonconstant
     ⇔ t_00 = t_01; constant response ⇒ trivially satisfied); union-find
     closure groups the free variables; S is affine in the group variables over
     the box [½−F, ½+F]; the max of an affine function over a box is attained
     at a vertex ⇒ endpoint sign patterns per group suffice (1312 candidates
     total — consistent with audit1.out L93); an affine A+BF ≤ 2 on [0,½] iff
     both endpoints ≤ 2 (audit1.py L296) ✓; S = 2 is attained at F = 0 by any
     local deterministic strategy ✓. Sound. The one-sided-NS side finding is
     correctly marked "not needed for any claim".

B.8  Theorem 5 (NS headline, all N ≥ 3) — CONSTRUCTION INDEPENDENTLY RE-
     DERIVED; ONE TYPO FOUND (P2-6).
     Lower bound: S_NS(N,F) ≤ S_max(N,F) and Corollary 2 ⇒ F*_NS(N) ≥
     (√2−1)/min(N,4) ✓ (trivial, correct).
     N≥4 witness — every component verified by hand: the per-class gauge gives
     patterns M_A, M_B, M_C, M_D for classes 0..3 ✓; row sums: n_r·x[ab,r] =
     −d with a compensating +d on one other class ⇒ each row sums to 1 ✓;
     per-row TV = ½(d+d) = d exactly, bang-bang in the σ_ab direction ✓;
     feasibility p ≥ 0 ⟺ n_r ≥ dN for all r ⟺ ⌊N/4⌋ ≥ (√2−1)N/4 (same case
     check as B.4) ✓; ALL FOUR NS identities computed explicitly: a=0 side —
     row 00 over classes {0,1}: −d+d = 0 = row 01's d−d ✓; a=1 side — row 10
     over {1,2}: d−d = 0 = row 11's 0+0 ✓; b=0 side (class 1): row 00 +d =
     row 10 +d ✓; b=1 side (class 0): row 01 +d = row 11 +d ✓. Value: S =
     S0 + 8d = 2 + 8F* = 2√2 with TV_ab = d for all ab ✓. Machine verification:
     ns_general.out Part A (exact Fractions, N=4..64) and Part C (float spot
     checks N=5,7,10,24: S to 1e-12, NS residuals ≤ 1.7e-16).
     N=3 witness — referee re-derived the Q(√2) table by hand using the saved
     gauge ns_solN3_{u,v}.npy: row sums = 1; per-row TV = (d3, d3, d3/2, d3);
     E[ab] = (⅓+2d3, ⅓+2d3, 1, −⅓−2d3); S = 2 + 6d3 = 2√2 EXACTLY; all four
     NS residuals = 0. Matches ns_general.out Part B/C (5.6e-17 vs the saved
     LP witness).
     TYPO: PROOFS §9.5 says "patterns {M_A, M_C, M_D}" but the ns_solN3 gauge
     gives per-state patterns {M_A, M_B, M_D} — state products (−,+,+,−),
     (+,−,+,−), (+,+,+,+); no CHSH symmetry maps one set to the other. The
     table and theorem are unaffected (both hand-verified). See P2-6.
     Gauge caveat paragraph (§9.5): correct and important — NS is not
     invariant under the per-state sign-flip gauge (it fixes q but changes
     single-party marginals); witnesses must specify full (u,v). Confirmed.

